= Emergence — Technical =

== Coarse-graining ==
Emergence is often analyzed through a mapping from microstate descriptions to macrostate variables:

<pre>
microstates → coarse-graining → macrostate
</pre>

Macro-level regularities can be stable even when many distinct microstates realize them.

== Explanatory levels ==
A macrodescription can have predictive/explanatory value even when the underlying dynamics are known.

This does not by itself establish strong metaphysical irreducibility.

== Relation to complexity ==
Nonlinearity, feedback, interaction topology, stochasticity, and scale separation can all support emergent behavior.

No single mechanism defines emergence across all fields.

